; Secret of Evermore: Casual Run -- version 2.4
; Single-file address-ordered source and native ROM reference.
; The active org/db payload rebuilds the approved v2.4 ROM; annotations emit no bytes.
;
; READING ORDER
; Canonical ROM addresses increase throughout the body, bank $C0 through $FF.
; Each bank begins with a functional summary and native/expansion byte counts.
; Native routines, tables, map records and script entry notes sit at their actual
; ROM locations between patch blocks. Functional headings are local to an address;
; they never move a function's bytes to a thematic appendix.
; Unchanged native code/data is inherited from the required clean ROM, not emitted
; again. A comment heading for a native address does not imply an org/db write.
; This is a complete PATCH plus a verified reference, not a full native disassembly.
; Unclassified code/data remains labelled honestly; no zero region is certified free.
;
; COORDINATES AND BUILD CONTRACT
; PC = canonical CPU - $C00000. Native $8F946B mirrors canonical $CF946B, PC $0F946B.
; This formula does not convert WRAM/SRAM/hardware addresses or packed VM pointers.
; Original unheadered USA image: $300000 bytes; output: $400000 bytes.
; Banks $C0-$EF are original ROM; $F0-$FF are added storage, including zero padding.
; UNCHANGED/MIXED applies only to a bounded interval compared against the clean ROM;
; unchanged helpers may still be called differently or consume patched data.
; RAM addresses below are runtime state, not ROM placements or save-file offsets.
; The build has no ASM includes or external documentation dependency.
; Commentary is self-contained; only the org/db statements below emit bytes.
; Reorganizing comments and db line boundaries preserves all original patch writes.
; An explicit final zero at $FFFFFF also fixes the output size for direct assemblers.
;
; RUNTIME-ONLY CROSS REFERENCES (not ROM addresses)
; REF_ACTOR_LAYOUT (WRAM, not ROM addresses):
;   Boy base $7E4E89; Dog base $7E4F37; actor update receives Y=actor base.
;   $7E3DDF is the active actor list head; $7E3DE3 is the free-list head.
;   Observed core offsets: +$0C palette selector, +$10/+12 actor control flags,
;   +$1A/+1C world position, +$22 direction, +$2A current HP, +$2E charge,
;   +$5E linked-list next actor, +$60 native combat/animation record selector.
;   These are selected fields, not a declaration that every record is identical.
;   Do not derive NPC allocation stride from the Boy/Dog address separation.
;
; Native long-indexed record accesses use $8E0000+X. The Boy and Dog selectors
; $0A26/$0A70 address LOW-WRAM MIRRORS, whereas high selectors can address ROM.
; Treating every record selector as a PC offset is wrong. The clone's $7E00
; sentinel/private SRAM record is an extension; patched record readers handle it.
;
; REF_INVENTORY_FLAGS (WRAM): $2262 bit $0004 Magic Gourd, bit $0010 Oracle Bone,
;   bit $0002 Jaguar Ring. $2261 bits 0/1 are Dog/Boy absence gates in this hack.
;   Do not use these bit numbers interchangeably with event-VM bit indexes.
; REF_PROGRESS_RAM (WRAM): Boy EXP $0A49 (24 bits), Dog EXP $0A93 (24 bits),
;   Dog level $0A9A, Dog skill $0B07, Dog HP $4F61; next Dog threshold $4FCB
;   (24 bits). These addresses are not offsets inside a battery save file.
;
; REFERENCE PROVENANCE
; Evidence sources and extension rules
; ------------------------------------
; Byte-identity labels: local clean USA ROM versus the complete current ASM.
; Engine notes: selected native instruction traces and earlier controlled Dog,
; clone, item-menu and reward fixtures, checked against this exact release.
; Map/text packing and table layouts: black-sliver / neagix, SoEScriptDumper;
; local reference sources match the Git blob IDs in the pinned upstream files:
;   commit d5ac6f390a50e6aa8c59a1c410e6affe49feb8f2
;   list-rooms.cpp blob 227376efe37e9918a005401632abe982c25ed7d2
;   data.h blob ff8f7a9d163064a762741bd2bb384dcef71583cf
;   https://github.com/black-sliver/SoEScriptDumper/tree/d5ac6f390a50e6aa8c59a1c410e6affe49feb8f2
; Further research index (not proof that a particular byte range is decoded):
;   https://github.com/black-sliver/SoETilesViewer
;   https://github.com/black-sliver/evermizer
;   https://datacrystal.tcrf.net/wiki/Secret_of_Evermore/ROM_map
;   https://datacrystal.tcrf.net/wiki/Secret_of_Evermore/RAM_map
;
; When extending this reference, identify CPU/PC/WRAM/VM coordinates explicitly;
; record native bytes, width/bank preconditions, callers and pointer consumers;
; separate observed behavior from inferred labels; then prove unchanged ROM and
; IPS output for documentation-only edits. Do not add speculative org/db writes.
;
; Clean SHA-256: 17c864a76d498feb6479eee8e7d6807b951c66225033228622bb66754baab1db
; Built SHA-256: 620b6cde35ac77966f6ee1988561be38e4b848ae33dd9fed7612c0d8e6dda1c9
; Sniff rewards: Prehistoric 10/4; Sacred 100/2; Poodle 1000/1.

arch 65816
hirom

; HOW TO READ THE CHANGE COMMENTS
; CHANGE explains an intent or before/after effect that has a verified source.
; SYMBOLIC lines restore readable labels/instructions from matching release sources;
; they are comments, not a second copy of executable code. Labels beginning with a
; routine name belong to that routine. Native/VM addresses are identified explicitly.
; NATIVE BYTES shows what an original-ROM patch replaces; it may be only part of an
; instruction or table entry. It is not presented as a complete disassembly.
; STORED TEXT is a printable preview with surrounding display controls omitted.
; NATIVE MATCH is a verified byte-identical source block, not a guessed asset type.
; Unidentified patches remain marked UNDECODED rather than assigned a false purpose.
; These annotations describe the cumulative 2.4 patch, not only changes since 2.3.
; Byte comparisons alone do not identify a feature; unattributed sites still need
; reverse engineering. The explanatory helper listings were recovered from the
; matching saved release sources and checked by reassembling those overlays.
;

