; @ROM $C085FA | PC $0085FA | NATIVE FUNCTION: palette DMA
; REF_DMA_PALETTE: $C085FA-$C0864F (mirror $8085FA).
;   Native palette transfer helper, reused by the clone and Dog visual effect.
;   With D=0, DP $26/$28 supplies a 24-bit source, DP $2E the CGRAM color index,
;   and X the byte count. Call with the native 16-bit register convention and a
;   hardware-accessible DB (existing callers use $80). It selects immediate DMA
;   or queues a request using $0106. Queued records start at $1292, seven bytes
;   per request; $128E is the producer offset. It uses DMA channel 1, can clobber
;   A/X/DP scratch, and returns with 16-bit A/X. Preserve caller state as needed.

; @ROM $C085FA | PC $0085FA | VERIFIED INTERVAL: Palette DMA helper
; CPU $C085FA-$C0864F; PC $0085FA-$00864F; UNCHANGED.
; The classification covers this bounded interval only, not its callees or pointed-to data.

; @ROM $C08650 | PC $008650 | NATIVE FUNCTION: VRAM DMA
; REF_DMA_VRAM: $C08650-$C086B1 (mirror $808650).
;   Similar immediate/queued transfer for VRAM; $2E is a VRAM WORD address,
;   $26/$28 the source, X the BYTE length. Queue at $013F, eight-byte requests,
;   producer offset $013D. This helper configures VMAIN increment-after-high-byte
;   mode. Do not write $2116/$2118 directly during active display to replace it.
;   Neither helper establishes a general re-entrancy or arbitrary-bank guarantee.

; @ROM $C08650 | PC $008650 | VERIFIED INTERVAL: VRAM DMA helper
