; @ROM $CCBBB0 | PC $0CBBB0 | NATIVE DATA / MENU: rare-item ownership and display
; REF_CHARMS: $CCBBB0 holds native rare-item ownership addresses; $CCBBD8 their
;   masks. $CCBC1A supplies names. $CCC334-$CCC38A renders owned-item icons.
;   Native descriptions use the word table at $CCC3D0, with strings in bank $C4.
;   The selection-to-description setup $CCC3BB is hooked for Gourd/Oracle only;
;   the rest of the menu remains inherited. Native names and older description
;   storage still exist even where a new pointer bypasses them.

; @ROM $CCBBB0 | PC $0CBBB0 | VERIFIED INTERVAL: Rare-item ownership addresses
; CPU $CCBBB0-$CCBBD7; PC $0CBBB0-$0CBBD7; UNCHANGED.
