; @ROM $D1F32E | PC $11F32E | NATIVE DATA / FORMAT: text dictionaries
; REF_TEXT_DICTIONARIES (native compressed stream):
;   $D1F32E: paired-character dictionary; $D1F3AE: single-character dictionary.
;   $D1F3EC: word-index table #1, string base $D1F66C.
;   $D1F46C: word-index table #2, string base $D1F7D5.
;   $C0 followed by an index chooses dictionary #2. Other $C1-$FF bytes select
;   dictionary #1; $40-$7F introduce literal runs. $80-$BF select character pairs,
;   $00-$3F select single characters. Display controls exist inside decoded text.
;   Decompress before treating text bytes as printable dialogue. Raw ASCII item
;   descriptions are a separate menu path and are not dictionary-compressed.

