; @ROM $D28000 | PC $128000 | NATIVE FORMAT: event VM header and script pointers
; REF_VM_BASE: canonical $D28000 (mirror $928000).
;   Packed event pointer p resolves to
;     $928000 + (p & $007FFF) + ((p & $FF8000) << 1).
;   Convert the resolved CPU mirror to a PC offset only AFTER this step.
;   This packing is not a direct 24-bit CPU pointer. Example: $155000 resolves
;   to $BCD000, canonical $FCD000. Native opcodes are not 65816 instructions.
;   Header word at +$00 locates the map/NPC callable-pointer table relative to
;   VM_BASE. Header word +$08 is the additional displacement to global pointers.
;   Native tables therefore start at $D28294 and $D2990B for this USA base.
;   Table contents and many called scripts are patched; layout is retained.
;   Enter-script pointer for map id is at VM_BASE+$1B+5*id (three pointer bytes).

